## 10. Can GitHub Pages Host Multiple Websites?

**Yes.** You can host multiple project websites under one GitHub account.

For example:

| Repository | Website |
|------------|---------|
| `emon.github.io` | `emon.github.io` |
| `QDoc` | `emon.github.io/QDoc/` |
| `Markdown-Editor` | `emon.github.io/Markdown-Editor/` |
| `PDF-Tools` | `emon.github.io/PDF-Tools/` |
| `Documentation` | `emon.github.io/Documentation/` |

You can also configure custom domains for individual sites.

This means you can maintain one central personal website and separate websites for your individual software projects.

---

## 11. Can You Use Databases, APIs and Backend Functionality?

This is an important limitation.

**GitHub Pages does not provide a server-side runtime.**

| Functionality | GitHub Pages |
|---------------|-------------|
| HTML/CSS/JS | Yes |
| Client-side routing | Yes |
| LocalStorage | Yes |
| IndexedDB | Yes |
| Fetch external APIs | Yes |
| Static JSON files | Yes |
| PHP backend | No |
| Node.js server | No |
| Python backend | No |
| MySQL database | No |
| Private environment variables in frontend | No |

However, you can connect your website to **external services**:

```
GitHub Pages website
HTML + CSS + JavaScript
        │
        ▼
HTTPS API requests
        │
        ├── Supabase (Database and authentication)
        ├── Firebase (Database and authentication)
        ├── Cloudflare Workers (Server-side functions)
        └── External APIs (Third-party services)
```

For example, you could build a complete Markdown editor, PDF converter interface, or GitHub repository browser on GitHub Pages.

&gt; **Remember:** API secrets must **never** be embedded in public JavaScript files. Put secret credentials in a secure backend or serverless function.

---

## 12. Important GitHub Pages Limitations

GitHub Pages is excellent for static websites, but it has usage restrictions.

| Limitation | Documented Guideline |
|------------|---------------------|
| Published site size | 1 GB |
| Soft bandwidth limit | 100 GB/month |
| Build time | 10 minutes |
| Deployment frequency | Generally no more than 10 builds per hour |
| Website type | Static websites |
| HTTPS | Supported |
| Custom domains | Supported |

&gt; These are published GitHub Pages limits and guidelines, **not a promise of unlimited production hosting**. Check the current official documentation for exceptions and details.

**Other considerations:**

- No native server-side application execution.
- No built-in database.
- No built-in user account system.
- No private API secret storage in client-side code.
- Large dynamic applications may need external services.

**Official documentation:** [GitHub Pages limits](https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/github-pages-limits)

