## 14. Common GitHub Pages Problems and Solutions

| Problem | Possible Solution |
|---------|-------------------|
| 404 error | Check `index.html` and publishing source |
| CSS not loading | Check file paths and capitalization |
| JavaScript not loading | Verify script paths |
| Website not updating | Check Actions deployment status |
| Blank page | Inspect browser console |
| Images not appearing | Verify relative paths |
| Custom domain not working | Check DNS records |
| HTTPS unavailable | Wait for certificate provisioning |
| React routes return 404 | Configure SPA fallback routing |
| Jekyll build failure | Inspect build logs and dependencies |

### Important Project Website Issue: Relative Paths

Suppose your project URL is:

```
https://emon.github.io/QDoc/
```

**Avoid** writing:

```html

```

This requests:

```
https://emon.github.io/script.js
```

**Instead, use:**

```html

```

Or configure your build tool's base path correctly.

This is especially important for Vite, React and Vue applications deployed under a repository subdirectory.

For Vite, for example:

```javascript
// vite.config.js

import { defineConfig } from "vite";

export default defineConfig({
  base: "/QDoc/"
});
```

If you use a custom domain at the root, your base path may instead be `/`.

